{"name":"Hindsight","hex":"#bdc9e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hindsight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Realization or understanding of the significance and nature of events after they have occurred.","The rear sight of a firearm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hindsight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hindsight (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Hindsight is an American comedy-drama television series that premiered on VH1 on January 7, 2015, and ended on March 11, 2015. The series was created by Emily Fox and stars Laura Ramsey in the lead role of Becca Brady. Becca wishes she had lived her life differently, and finds herself sent back to 1995, with her knowledge and experience and a chance to do things differently."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/Hindsight_intertitle.png/330px-Hindsight_intertitle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindsight_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q18786444"},{"title":"Hindsight (2011 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Hindsight is a 2011 South Korean action drama film by Lee Hyun-seung, his first after a ten-year hiatus. The film is about a hitwoman who struggles with her feelings for the underworld boss who is her target. The film deals with issues of age difference, and the Korean underworld. It stars Song Kang-ho and Shin Se-kyung, and premiered at the 16th Busan International Film Festival. The film received a total of 763,776 admissions nationwide."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Hindsight_%282011_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindsight_(2011_film)","wikidata":"Q5766239"},{"title":"Hindsight bias","blocks":[{"text":"Hindsight bias, also known as the knew-it-all-along phenomenon or creeping determinism, is the common tendency for people to perceive past events as having been more predictable than they were."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindsight_bias","wikidata":"Q1960297"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Craig_Horner_and_Laura_Ramsey_on_Trending_Report.jpg/500px-Craig_Horner_and_Laura_Ramsey_on_Trending_Report.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Craig_Horner_and_Laura_Ramsey_on_Trending_Report.jpg/1280px-Craig_Horner_and_Laura_Ramsey_on_Trending_Report.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Craig_Horner_and_Laura_Ramsey_on_Trending_Report.jpg/500px-Craig_Horner_and_Laura_Ramsey_on_Trending_Report.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Craig Horner and Laura Ramsey discuss Hindsight in 2015","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACraig_Horner_and_Laura_Ramsey_on_Trending_Report.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daniel_Kahneman_%283283955327%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Daniel_Kahneman_%283283955327%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Daniel_Kahneman_%283283955327%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Daniel_Kahneman_%283283955327%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Daniel Kahneman, who researched hindsight bias","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADaniel_Kahneman_(3283955327)_(cropped).jpg"}],"sounds":{"hindsight":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-hindsight.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/6c/LL-Q1860_%